[[File:Pontevedra CF - AD Ceuta FC, Primeira División RFEF 2022-23 a 58.jpg|right|thumb|Match between [[Pontevedra CF|Pontevedra]] and [[AD Ceuta FC|Ceuta]] on 26 February 2023, at the [[Estadio Municipal de Pasarón|Pasarón]]]]
The '''2022–23 Primera Federación''' season was the second season for the [[Primera Federación]], the third highest level in the [[Spanish football league system]]. Forty teams participated, divided into two groups of twenty clubs each based on geographical proximity. In each group, the champions were automatically promoted to [[Segunda División]], while the second to fifth placers played the promotion play-offs and the bottom five were relegated to the [[Segunda Federación]].

==Overview before the season==
A total of 40 teams joined the league, including four relegated from the [[2021–22 Segunda División]], 26 retained from the [[2021–22 Primera División RFEF]], and 10 promoted from the [[2021–22 Segunda División RFEF]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://as.com/futbol/2022/05/21/mas_futbol/1653149930_687830.html|title=Playoff de Segunda y Tercera RFEF: partidos y resultados de la fase de ascenso|trans-title=Segunda and Tercera RFEF play-offs: matches and results from the promotion phase|publisher=[[Diario AS]]|language=es|date=22 May 2022|accessdate=22 May 2022}}</ref>

